{"id":"word:hebrew:H403","type":"word","title":"אָכֵן","subtitle":"H403 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"firmly ; figuratively, surely ; also (adversative) but","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אָכֵן (H403) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: adv.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 18 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אָכֵן (ʼâkên) means firmly ; figuratively, surely ; also (adversative) but First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 11 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אָכֵן","transliteration":"ʼâkên","pronunciation":"aw-kane'","strong":"H403","lemmaId":"hebrew:H403","partOfSpeech":"adv","forms":["אָכֵן֙","אָ֭כֵן","אָכֵ֖ן","אָכֵ֥ן","אָכֵ֕ן"],"morphs":[["HD",18]]},"definitions":{"short":"firmly ; figuratively, surely ; also (adversative) but","usage":"but, certainly, nevertheless, surely, truly, verily.","full":"H403. aken אָכֵן (perhaps from אַח ; compare Aramaic דֵּח & דִּכֵּן ) adverb with strong asseverative force: a. surely, truly , especially at beginning of a speech (stronger & more decided than אַח ) Gen 28:16 ; Exod 2:14 ; 1Sam 15:32 ; Isa 40:7 ; 45:15 ; Jer 3:23 (twice in verse); 4:10 ; 8:8 . In 1Kin 11:2 אָבֵן stands unusually; and מֶּןֿ (compare ᵑ7 ᵑ6 ᵐ5 ) should probably be read (so Klo). b. emphasizing a contrast , but indeed, but in fact , especially after אָמַרְתִּי I said or thought , expressing the reality, in opposed to what had been wrongly imagined, Isa 49:4 b (opposed to v a ) 53:4 (opposed to 53:3 end) Jer 3:20 (opposed to the expectation 3:19 b) Zeph 3:7 b Psa 31:23 b (opposed to 31:23 a) 66:19 ; 82:7 (opposed to 82:6 ) Job 32:8 (opposed to 32:7 ).","rootNote":"from 3559 (compare 3651 );","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 11 2","keyReferences":["1Kgs 11 2","1Sam 15 32","Exod 2 14","Gen 28 16","Isa 40 7","Isa 45 15","Isa 49 4","Isa 53 4"],"related":{"people":[],"